  "count": 3,
  "rationale": "Block browserStore:credentialAccess, printServer:lateralMovement and backupHost:lateralMovement. (1) Blocking browserStore cuts appServer, because all three of its parents depend on browserStore. It also cuts dbLogin, which in turn kills domainAdmin and dbReplica. (2) Blocking printServer kills hypervisor, which needs printServer AND jumpHost. That leaves codeRepo with no live parent. (3) Blocking backupHost kills serviceAccount and secretsManager, which kills vaultRead. With printServer also blocked, shareMount has no live parent. All four target parents are now dead. Two blocks cannot work. The printServer path into shareMount must be cut by tokenCache, printServer or shareMount itself. None of these, paired with any single other step, also cuts the backupHost/vaultRead branch, dbReplica and the appServer path into codeRepo. So the minimum is 3."
